**Play now:** https://critical-drug-fraser-spending.trycloudflare.com

**What it is:** Cube Tapper (\`./index.html\`, zero dependencies) — click/tap the orbiting cube before the 30s timer ends. Space = tap, R = restart, live score/hit/accuracy HUD. Every load also probes and displays the real GPU renderer string, so the game itself is the interactive 3D workload behind the hardware verdict.

**Final commit:** \`305eaf0\` — *Add Cube Tapper playable WebGL game with GPU diagnostics, reports, and final screenshots* — pushed to branch \`opencode/34309443121\` ([compare/view](https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/tree/opencode/34309443121)).

**Screenshots (captured headless Chrome 152 against the public URL, committed under \`screenshots/\`):**

Gameplay:
![final public game](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/opencode/34309443121/screenshots/final-public-game.png)

Self-test evidence page:
![final public selftest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/opencode/34309443121/screenshots/final-public-selftest.png)

**Deployment status:** public Cloudflare tunnel URL returns \`200 OK\` and renders byte-identical frames to local \`:3000\` (tmux \`app-server\` session, persistent per Agents.md). Local self-test page title \`SELFTEST-PASS\`.

**Test status:** 11/11 browser PASS, 0 failures — canvas-present, webgl-context (WebGL 2.0), renderer \`ANGLE (Apple, ANGLE Metal Renderer: Apple Paravirtual device)\`, no-software-renderer, hw-gated-context (\`failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat\` OK), framebuffer-readback, pixelhook-positive, direct-hit-scores, miss-penalized, restart-resets, hud-synced. Full diagnostics in \`GPU_REPORT.md\` / \`GPU_PROGRESS.md\` on the branch.

**Known limitations:**
- WebGPU is PARTIAL: \`navigator.gpu\` present but \`requestAdapter\` hangs in display-less headless runs (all backends); needs a headed-desktop retest for a full WebGPU verdict — headed path documented in \`GPU_REPORT.md\`.
- Headless \`-screenshot\` captures DOM/HUD reliably; raw WebGL canvas pixels are proven via in-page \`readPixels\` rather than the PNG alone.
- This VM exposes a paravirtual Apple GPU, not discrete hardware — the claim is hardware-vs-software rendering path, not discrete-GPU performance.
- The public tunnel URL is ephemeral (trycloudflare); the durable artifact is branch \`opencode/34309443121\` commit \`305eaf0\`." 2>&1
